cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WolfPackR, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "WolfPackR: Identifying wolf packs based on genetic and spatial data"
abstract: >-
  R package that delineates wolf packs, and the status of each individual, from
  pairwise relatedness and the locations of non-invasive genetic samples.
  Families are found by community detection on the relatedness graph, the space
  use of each individual is estimated by kernel density with a common bandwidth,
  each individual is assigned to the territory where most of its samples fall
  with an explicit status, and families spread over several territories are
  split into spatially coherent packs. It also computes relatedness from
  microsatellite genotypes, describes packs including land tenure metrics, and
  measures agreement with a reference and robustness to settings and sampling
  effort.
authors:
  - family-names: Boncourt
    given-names: Etienne
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8233-0190"
